A stub key can be the dotted path plus the call arguments, so one macro can be stubbed per argument
list: the call carrying those arguments takes the stub, and the bare call falls through to the real
`date`, whose reading is wildcarded.

-- fixtures/cwd/probe.md.j2 --
pinned {{ macro('core.macros.date', '+%Y%m%d%H%M') }}
live {{ macro('core.macros.date', '+booped-%Y') }}
-- cmd --
booping render /proc/self/cwd/probe.md.j2 --stub-macro "core.macros.date +%Y%m%d%H%M=197001010000"
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
pinned 197001010000
live booped-[..]
-- stderr --
